        "procedure": "At room temperature, Eu(OAc)3·6H2O (0.20 mmol, 0.0874 g), CdCl2 (0.20 mmol, 0.0366 g), ZnCl2 (0.20 mmol, 0.0272 g) and HL (0.20 mmol, 0.0332 g) were dissolved in ethanol (6 mL) and methanol (4 mL). Triethylamine (1.0 mol/L) in 1 mL of ethanol was added. The mixture was stirred under reflux for 30 min, cooled to room temperature, and filtered. Slow diffusion of diethyl ether into the filtrate afforded yellow crystals of 1.",
