      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "optical",
        "summary": "Cluster 1 shows typical Eu(III) 5D0→7Fj luminescence in CH3CN with a weak ligand-centered emission near 485 nm upon 395 nm excitation; the strongest line is at 615 nm (5D0→7F2) with τ = 29.84 μs. MLX enhances the Eu emission (I615 more than fivefold at 60 μM MLX) with a linear calibration I615 nm = 3060 × [MLX] + 46604 (k = 3.065×10^3 μM−1), LOD 2.31×10−2 nM, and response time ≤5 s. Paper strips of 1 turn red under UV with MLX, enabling qualitative and quantitative sensing of MLX including in tablets.",
